              "text": "Construct residual and flux arrays from rational-string patterns; verify item counts match schema (3 arrays for residual, 2 for edge_flux, 3 for density_derivative/source).",
              "failure_or_gain": "gain"
            },
            {
              "kind": "antibody",
              "text": "The fixture H=[[0,1,0],[1,0,1],[0,1,0]], P=diag(1,0,0), ψ=(1,i,1) yields total defect density ν_0+ν_1+ν_2 = 2. Edge fluxes F_{0→1}=[1,0], F_{1→2}=[0,1] give net outflow 1, so total defect is not conserved: d/dt(2) = 0 but flux imbalance 1 ≠ 0 source. This is the counterexample to unconditional conservation.",
              "failure_or_gain": "gain"
            }
          ],
